WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:07.360
There’s something about the experimental
nature of science that attracts the crazies.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.559
You just won’t believe what despicable,
weird and just downright evil things these

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:19.340
pioneers of the bizarre have done.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.050
1.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.779
Sergei S. Bryukhonenko, was a Soviet scientist,
and head of the Research Institute of Experimental

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:31.220
Surgery, during the Stalin era.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.090
Now that’s a recipe for a mad scientist
if ever I heard one.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:40.080
Sergei was the inventor of the first artificial
heart machine, which he called the autojektor,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.760
a machine that’s purpose was to sustain
life through artificial means.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.130
It was used to help perform the first Soviet
open heart surgery.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:54.870
Seems to be going pretty well so far doesn’t
it, well this is the bit where it goes weird.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:01:00.150
Sergei was obsessed with mutilating animals
then seeing how long he could keep their dismembered

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.760
heads alive.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.479
His laboratory was filled with dead, mostly
headless, dogs.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:08.259
I told you it gets weird.

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:13.890
Sergei’s most infamous experiment was documented
on video and it involved decapitating a dog,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.889
which he then placed on a table.

00:01:15.889 --> 00:01:21.799
Sergei then managed to bring the head back
to life using his homemade life support machine.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:26.930
The severed dog’s head was fully responsive
and it even accepted a treat from the staff.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.100
The original recording of the experiment can
be found on the internet, but I should warn

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.229
you it’s not for the faint hearted.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:34.229
2.

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:39.389
During World War II, thousands of human experiments
were carried out by nazi scientists under

00:01:39.389 --> 00:01:40.909
Hitler’s instruction.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:46.100
The goal of these experiments was to discover
new ways to aid German military personnel

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:51.069
whom had been injured during combat, and also
to discover radical new medical treatments

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.329
to advance Hitler’s ideology.

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:56.210
The leader of these experiments was Dr. Josef
Mengele.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.119
Who earned himself the nickname the “Angel
of Death” for the atrocities he carried

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:02.119
out.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.380
When new inmates arrived at Auschwitz, Mengele
would select which were to be gassed and which

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.970
would be taken to the laboratory to conduct
his inhumane experiments on.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:17.570
Josef Mergele was obsessed by twins, he would
often attempt to stitch the flesh, blood vessels

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:22.190
and organs of twins together in an attempt
to create Siamese twins.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:28.240
But his subjects often contracted gangrene
and died after a couple of days of unimaginable

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.240
pain.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:34.570
Josef performed experiments such as putting
victims into pressure chambers, castration,

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:41.170
freezing subjects to death, removal of organs
and limbs and even performing sex change operations.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.240
Most of the victims were murdered following
the experiment, if they didn’t straight

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.670
up die from the experiment that is.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.670
3.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:53.180
During the second Sino-Japanese War and World
War II the Imperial Japanese Army setup a

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:59.570
covert biological and chemical research and
development base called Unit 731.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.290
They told the locals it was a water treatment
plant, but that guise must have fallen apart

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.820
pretty quickly once the locals realised that
the screams of tortured humans sounds remarkably

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.910
different than running water.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:17.590
Microbiologist, and medical officer Shirō
Ishii, was the director of Unit 731.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:23.880
He committed numerous atrocities at Unit 731,
in the name of science, including: vivisection

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:30.320
of living people without anaesthetic, including
pregnant women, dismembering peoples limbs

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.260
then reattaching them to other parts of their
body, injecting subjects with deadly diseases

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:42.790
to study the effects and even using people
as live test targets for grenades and flame

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:43.790
throwers.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:49.460
However after the war ended Shirō Ishii never
spent any time in jail for his atrocities,

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.490
because he was granted immunity by the US
government.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:57.190
Some believe this is because the US made a
pact with Japan during the war to help cover

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:01.670
up Unit 731, in exchange for medical knowledge
of their findings.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.670
4.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:09.900
At number 4 is Sidney Gottlieb, but he had,
possibly the coolest alias of all the evil

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.930
scientists, his colleagues referred to him
as Dr. Feelgood.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.220
He was an American military psychiatrist with
a Ph.D in chemistry.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:25.510
During the Cold War the CIA hired him to help
develop biological weapons and poisons to

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.000
use against the Russians.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.320
But Gottlieb’s only answer to taking out
America’s enemies was to poison them all.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:38.040
Gottlieb proposed the idea of killing Fidel
Castro with either a poisoned cigar, a poisoned

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:44.820
fountain pen, or a poisoned wetsuit, whichever
was easiest, it turns out none was the answer,

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:45.840
since he’s still alive.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.770
Gottlieb’s other unsuccessful poisoning
attempts included an Iraqi general and the

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.610
prime minister of the Democratic Republic
of the Congo.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.940
But that’s just the tip of Sidney Gottlieb’s
weird iceberg.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.460
He was also the head of the MKULTRA project.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.080
Which studied the possibility of using LSD
to mind control one’s enemies.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.440
They were interested if the psychedelic drug
could be used to break a person’s mind for

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.060
the purpose of interrogation.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.810
So Gottlieb and his colleague’s spent a
large portion of their time getting high on

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:18.810
acid.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.370
But they soon realised they would need test
subjects other than themselves.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:28.650
However instead of inviting willing subjects
to get high on LSD, Gottlieb instead travelled

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:34.230
around America slipping LSD into people’s
drinks and observing the effects.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.290
He mainly targeted prostitutes and drug addicts.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.290
5.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:44.300
Next up is American psychologist, Harry Harlow,
he had the nickname “Monkey Torturer”,

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.270
you just know that this guy qualifies for
this video with a name like that.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:55.400
He was obsessed with finding out “what is
love”, and for some unknown reason he decided

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.600
the best way to do that was by torturing baby
monkeys.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.840
Yes, that’s right baby monkeys.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.360
To achieve his goal Harlow invented a range
of monkey torturing devices.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:13.270
One of his most infamous, he lovingingly referred
to as the “rape rack”.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:17.610
Harlow would use his rape rack device to force
monkeys to mate.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.040
He also had a device he called the “iron
maiden”.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:25.420
But perhaps his most controversial experiment
was called the “pit of despair”.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:30.889
Harlow would place a baby monkey in a small
isolated chamber for up to a year, without

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:33.420
any contact with another living creature.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:42.120
As a result, the monkeys all became psychotic
and never recovered.

